# A6L thermal kernel fragment (thermal follow-up, 29 Sep 2026, docs/android-thermal-cooling-20260929.md). PROPOSED for the
# next kernel rebuild (r6). APPLIED 29 Sep 2026: kernel-r5-20260930 Image de4970b3 = r5 config + this fragment
# (kernel-r5-20260930/scripts/build-r5-thermal.sh; old Image 5f92e057 had DELAY_MS=0, kept in pre-thermal-20260929/).
# Why: r5 sets STATIC_USERMODEHELPER=y with an empty path (android-base). A critical thermal trip calls
# __hw_protection_trigger -> orderly_poweroff(true) -> run_cmd("/sbin/poweroff"): with an empty static path
# call_usermodehelper_exec returns 0 without running anything, so the "force" fallback (emergency_sync + kernel_power_off)
# never runs, and with DELAY_MS=0 no backup emergency poweroff is queued: on r5 a critical trip (CPU 110 C, GPU 110 C,
# PM660/PM660L 125 C) only logs "HARDWARE PROTECTION shutdown". (V67: no static UMH -> /sbin/poweroff is absent -> error ->
# forced kernel_power_off, i.e. safe.) A positive delay queues hw_failure_emergency_poweroff -> kernel_power_off.
# 100 ms = the Android GKI value.
CONFIG_THERMAL_EMERGENCY_POWEROFF_DELAY_MS=100
